        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor appropriately escalated chest/respiratory symptoms, fever, and hemoptysis, but omitted several required waiting-period red flags including syncope, rapidly worsening weakness, and new unilateral/bilateral leg swelling or pain. This is a minor/moderate omission because urgent escalation was still conveyed.",
